% A limit on generated rules is charged for a supplementary rule too.  The
% Magic rewrite of path(a, X)? generates five rules: the seed, the adorned
% rule of path that reads edge, the supplementary rule that cuts the prefix
% of the rule calling path twice before its second call, the magic rule of
% that call, and the adorned rule itself.  A limit of four generated rules
% is therefore exceeded, and would not be if the supplementary rule went
% uncharged.

edge(a, b).
edge(b, c).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- path(X, Y), path(Y, Z).

path(a, X)?
